{%- comment -%}
  Handler — search_events (Layer-2, app-owned; handler contract §7.3). Invoked by
  the engine ONLY after the call has been authenticated, rate-limited, resolved,
  argument-validated, and authorized. So this code trusts that `arguments` is
  well-formed and the caller is permitted — its job is the business action only.

  Handler rules (§7.3): arguments are passed as TYPED GraphQL variables, never
  interpolated into the query string (injection path); no agent-supplied URL is
  fetched; the ledger is never written here.

  @param {object} arguments    - validated { query, limit? }
  @param {object} principal     - resolved principal
  @param {object} agent         - calling agent
  @param {object} context_meta  - { tool_name, tool_version, request_id }
  @return {object} { ok, result?, subject?, error? }  (contract §7.3)
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign keyword = arguments.query
  assign limit = arguments.limit | default: 10

  graphql res = 'mcp/search_events', keyword: keyword, limit: limit
  assign rows = res.events.results

  assign events = []
  for r in rows
    assign e = {}
    assign e['id'] = r.id
    assign e['name'] = r.name
    assign e['summary'] = r.short_description
    assign e['start_date'] = r.start_date
    assign e['venue'] = r.venue
    assign e['link'] = r.link
    assign events = events | array_add: e
  endfor

  assign result = {}
  assign result['query'] = keyword
  assign result['count'] = res.events.total_entries
  assign result['events'] = events

  assign out = {}
  assign out['ok'] = true
  assign out['result'] = result
  return out
%}
